      "content": "It sounds like your sourdough starter is fermenting too quickly, affecting the balance of your dough. Adjusting the ambient temperature is likely the best approach. Warmer temperatures (around 75°F/24°C) can cause the starter to ferment too rapidly, so consider moving it to a cooler spot. Additionally, maintaining a regular feeding schedule can help regulate the starter's fermentation rate. This will give you a better sense of when to feed and when to adjust the temperature.",
