      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i've been keeping it around 76 but maybe that's the issue. regarding the flour though, i've been using a standard unbleached all-purpose. would switching to a high protein bread flour actually help stabilize the pH, or does that just provide more fuel for the yeast to go crazy again? i'm trying to understand the actual chemistry of why the acidity shoots up so suddenly.",
